# Hook scripts must keep LF endings on every platform.
#
# A Windows checkout that rewrites .mjs to CRLF would not break Node, but the
# same habit applied to the shell canary would break its shebang — and a hook
# that fails to start exits non-zero, which Claude Code treats as a
# NON-BLOCKING error. The tool call then proceeds: the gate fails open silently.
# Pinning LF removes that whole class of failure.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
